{{/*
  claim-heartbeat — bare `claim_heartbeat_at` refresh, used by L2 drivers
  whose Step 0 already established the passive claim on a prior iteration
  and only needs to update the heartbeat timestamp this turn. This is a
  companion to `claim-entry.tmpl` — `claim-entry` handles first-claim +
  refresh; `claim-heartbeat` is the leaner form for callers that already
  did the claim/foreign-claim check via `claim-entry` (i.e. every L2
  loop-driver, since `claim-entry` is idempotent and covers both cases).

  Currently NOT invoked directly — `claim-entry` covers the heartbeat via
  its `claimed_by == self` branch, avoiding a double-write per iteration.
  Kept as a named fragment for two reasons:

    1. Future callers that want a pure heartbeat (no first-claim path)
       can invoke this without pulling in the foreign-claim / defer
       branches from `claim-entry`.
    2. Symmetry with `claim-clear.tmpl` — each side of the claim/refresh/
       clear lifecycle has a dedicated named fragment, so
       grep-and-audit ("who touches claim metadata?") is trivially
       answered by `rg 'claim-(entry|heartbeat|clear)'`.

  Usage — after Step 0's initial claim, once per iteration:

      {{ template "beads-issues/shared/claim-heartbeat" (dict
          "Target" $target
      ) }}

  Parameters:
    Target — the resolved bead ID (empty string skips the whole block).
*/}}
{{- if .Target }}
Refresh the claim heartbeat so the L1 reaper's staleness check treats this
driver as alive:

```bash
bd update {{ .Target }} --set-metadata "claim_heartbeat_at=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
```
{{- end }}
